Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/11/meet-the-2026-app-store-award-finalists/">revealed the 45 finalists</a> for its 2026 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a> Awards, with nominations spanning its devices, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-arcade/">Apple Arcade</a>, and the Cultural Impact category.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/12/Apple-App-Store-Awards-2025.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1029082" /><br/>
"ElevenReader," "(Not Boring) Camera," and "Raylie" are in contention for iPhone App of the Year. On the Mac, the app nominees are clipboard manager "Paste," task manager "Things 3," and writing app "Ulysses," while "Big Walk," "Blue Prince," and "Crimson Desert" are competing for the gaming award. The full list of finalists follows:<br/>
<br/>
<h4>iPhone App of the Year</h4><br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/elevenreader-read-books-aloud/id6479373050/">ElevenReader</a></strong>: A text-to-speech app with AI-generated narration.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/not-boring-camera/id6737783441/">(Not Boring) Camera</a></strong>: A customizable camera app inspired by vintage cameras.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/raylie-flight-view-guide/id6793443320/">Raylie</a></strong>: A flight companion that provides personalized guidance during journeys.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
<h4>iPhone Game of the Year</h4><br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/ball-x-pit/id6738703497/">BALL x PIT</a></strong>: A game that puts a twist on brick-breaking mechanics.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/dave-the-diver/id6759962259/">DAVE THE DIVER</a></strong>: An underwater adventure centered on diving and ocean exploration.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/gambonanza/id6747752407/">Gambonanza</a></strong>: A chess-inspired game that changes the traditional rules.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
<h4><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> App of the Year</h4><br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cosmos-search-discover/id1577975475/">Cosmos</a></strong>: A visual discovery app for collecting inspiration in mood boards.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/kiddopia-kids-learning-games/id1223397201/">Kiddopia</a></strong>: A collection of educational games and activities for young children.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/mockup-ui-ux-design/id1527554407/">Mockup</a></strong>: A design tool for planning app and website interfaces.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
<h4>&zwnj;iPad&zwnj; Game of the Year</h4><br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/aniimo/id6759098797/">Aniimo</a></strong>: A fantasy adventure featuring creature companions.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/arknights-endfield/id6752642477/">Arknights: Endfield</a></strong>: A science-fiction game with combat on a distant moon.</li><br/>
<li><strong><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/where-winds-meet/id6472396866/">Where Winds Meet</a></strong>: An adventure built around martial arts combat.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
<h4>Mac App of the Year</h4><br/>
<ul><br/>
